note patch/p1decl.om: git patch intake (docs/API.md "Git patches"). Every text and global of the slice,
note declared before any use. Prefixes: functions pa*, globals gp*, texts tp*.
note A patch is a `git format-patch --stdout BASE..HEAD` mbox with a title and a description, uploaded
note by the local command `interplane patch` (tools/bring) in one signed POST. The forge checks it,
note applies it once on BASE in a throwaway work tree and keeps the bytes under
note <data>patches/<owner>/<repo>/<id>/. It never writes a repository and never signs for anyone.
note Repositories are the bare git stores of the Interplane store this build reads,
note <store>projects/<name>/repo.git (store/repos.om, server/util.om fksdir); nothing here reads
note Radicle storage. The slice is composed only in a store-reading build (run.sh).
text tpsdir "patches/"
text tpindex "index"
text tptmp "tmp/"
text tppw "pw"
text tpfmb "mbox"
text tpfst "statement"
text tpfsg "signature"
text tpfhd "head"
text tpfss "status"
text tpftt "title"
text tpfds "description"
text tpfme "meta"
text tpfdf "diff"
text tpnewd ".new-"
text tpopen "open\n"
text tpwm "/m"
text tpww "/w"
text tpwalt "/w/.git/objects/info/alternates"
text tpobj "/objects\n"
text tpdot "."
text tpdd ".."
